{
  "dom_id": "question-218622",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "If $P$ is a statement, $\\text{t}$ is a tautology, and $\\text{c}$ is a contradiction, complete the following table of logical equivalences.\n\n| Statement | Is Logically Equivalent To |\n| --- | --- |\n| $\\text{t}∧\\text{t}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{t}∨\\text{c}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{c}∨¬P$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{t}∨P$ | {{field-4}} |",
